 "result": "The default session is a signed-cookie session. Typed values survive the JSON round trip because of a tagging serializer.\n\n- **`SignedCookieSessionInterface`** (`src/tessel/sessions.py`) is the default session interface. Its `serializer` attribute is `session_json_serializer`, and `make_signer` builds an itsdangerous `URLSafeTimedSerializer` that signs the payload.\n- **`TypedCookieSerializer`** (`src/tessel/json/tag.py`) is exposed as `session_json_serializer`. It tags tuples, bytes, Markup, UUID and datetime values, plus dicts that have a `\" di\"` key. On save it wraps each such value in a tagged JSON form, and on load it reverses the tag to restore the original type.\n- **`SignedCookieSession`** (`src/tessel/sessions.py`) is the session object itself, a `CallbackDict` with `SessionMixin`. It tracks `modified` and `accessed`.\n\nOn save, `finalize_reply` calls `persist_session`, which serializes and signs the session into the cookie. On load, `restore_session` verifies the signature and deserializes it.\n\nI took this from `brain/sessions.md` and did not open the source files.",
